    {
      "question": "q-36305",
      "field": null,
      "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
      "old_sha256": "7d6b238b5453fe04d4e9e589345510f00da07b7a74d0b73c47ab6818a6df9b7b",
      "new_sha256": "3a9087080106efa6bb6f2845427d2ebbf388a5bd5ae187f2a5b8e4e2c3b54e3c",
      "category": "ma_capture",
      "authoring": [],
      "source": [
        {
          "question": "q-36305",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "At a given point, a function $g(x,y,z)$ increases most rapidly in the direction of its gradient at that point.\n\nSo, we compute $\u2207g(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at the point $(1,1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207g(x,y,z) & =\u27e8\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}({y}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2\\pi x+\\pi z)),\\,\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}({y}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2\\pi x+\\pi z)),\\,\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z}({y}^{2}+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2\\pi x+\\pi z))\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e82\\pi \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2\\pi x+\\pi z),\\,2y,\\,\\pi \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2\\pi x+\\pi z)\u27e9 \\\\ \u2207g(1,1,2) & =\u27e82\\pi \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2\\pi \\cdot 1+\\pi \\cdot 2),\\,2\\cdot 1,\\,\\pi \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2\\pi \\cdot 1+\\pi \\cdot 2)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e82\\pi \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(4\\pi ),\\,2,\\,\\pi \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(4\\pi )\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e82\\pi ,\\,2,\\,\\pi \u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function increases most rapidly in the direction of $\u27e82\\pi ,\\,2,\\,\\pi \u27e9.$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14069662/state.json",
          "file_sha256": "4376702b89825ead4f855d51ff612fc2873c7f6e8d7c2ccea7cc869d52433740"
        }
      ],
